# SiYuan PoC Caddy - TLS (internal CA) + basicauth in front of the kernel.
# The kernel (siyuan:6806) is NOT published to the LAN; all traffic goes through here.
#
# SCOPE (ADR-0012 section 7): this file serves the SiYuan kernel and nothing else.
# It is a lab edge, not the product edge.
#
# Removed 2026-08-06 per ADR-0012 section 2 (reconciliation inconsistency 10):
#   handle_path /family*  -> 172.18.0.1:6902  (family_facade.py)
#   handle      /api*     -> 172.18.0.1:6903  (lifeos_api.py, the Ingest API)
# Both published a family-lifeos product surface from an experiment repo. The
# /api route now lives in family-lifeos/infra/compose/Caddyfile; the facade moved
# to family-lifeos/scripts/experimental/ and is run directly, not proxied here.
#
# Known limitation (Caddy 2.8): the internal cert is only served to clients that
# send the IP as SNI. Most browsers do; curl/python/PowerShell on Windows against
# a raw IP do not. For automation, hit the kernel through a client that sets SNI
# or use --insecure/--resolve in tests.

{$SITE_ADDRESS:192.168.88.9} {
    tls internal

    # NOTE: basicauth via `caddy hash-password` is unavailable in this image
    # (returns "Error: EOF" on the PoC host); auth is enforced by the SiYuan
    # lock screen (accessAuthCode). Re-enable basicauth in production once a
    # hash can be generated (see docs/adr/0001).
    reverse_proxy siyuan:6806 {
        header_up Host {host}
        header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
    }
}
